# Page chrome (mandatory)

Every screen mounted under `#app` must follow these rules. Do not invent one-off top spacing or header heights.

## 1. Phone status-bar safe area

- Content must never sit under the notch / Dynamic Island / status bar.
- Safe inset is applied on `#app` via CSS (`--safe-top` in desktop studio; `env(safe-area-inset-top)` on real devices). UI scale still comes from `uiScale.js`.
- **Do not** position page roots with `position: absolute; inset: 0` (that ignores `#app` padding and covers the safe area).
- Page roots use normal flex flow inside `#app` (`flex flex-col`, `flex-1 min-h-0` when visible).
- Full-screen overlays/modals that must clear the cutout use  
  `padding-top: max(var(--safe-top, 0px), env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px))` (or sit inside `#app` so they inherit the inset).

## 2. Page title bar (`.page-header`)

- **Every** page has a top title bar as the first child: `<header class="page-header">`.
- Size, padding, border, and title typography are defined only in `src/styles/main.css` for `.page-header` — do not override min-height / padding per page.
- Layout pattern (same on all pages):

```html
<header class="page-header">
  <!-- back button OR empty side slot -->
  <button type="button" class="page-header-side" …>…</button>
  <!-- OR --><span class="page-header-side" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <h1 class="page-header-title">Page Name</h1>
  <span class="page-header-side" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</header>
```

- Title text is concise English. Side slots are always `page-header-side` so the title stays optically centered and bar height matches across Home / tabs / DIY / Details.

## 3. Adaptive type & layout

- Prefer `rem` / Tailwind scale tokens; do not hard-code px font sizes that fight `uiScale`.
- New pages live under `src/pages/<name>/` and register in `src/main.js` + `src/shared/nav.js` when they are routes.
